---
title: One fx attempt for the Rex resume rule
---
stateDiagram-v2
    %% One fx process runs one attempt. Source: tests/tla/rex_rule/RexRule.tla, which follows src/core/rex_rule/.
    %% The branch (setting on or off) is read when the attempt takes the lock, and the attempt keeps it.
    %% Every write to init.lua is one atomic step that first compares init.lua with what the attempt observed.
    %% A change since the observation stops the attempt at once: no rollback, added and fx.lua stay as they are
    %% (fx.lua this attempt created is deleted on the add path).
    %% Rules checked on this chart: all five invariants hold (design and design-three, crashes and faults on).
    %% Events left out: the user's own rule text, a foreign line, a missing init.lua, a config check that fails before the
    %% attempt starts, a Rex restart, a user text edit that is not after the observation, cancellation of a record wait,
    %% other fx processes waiting on the lock, and a setting flip during an attempt (it affects only attempts that start later).
    %% A user removal does not reopen adds: only an off attempt that finds the line present clears added, so after a
    %% removal nothing clears it. The flip does not change this.
    [*] --> Working : lock free
    [*] --> Busy : lock held by another fx
    Busy --> [*]
    Working --> Crashed : process killed at any step (lock dropped, files stay as they are)
    Crashed --> [*]
    state Working {
        [*] --> Start
        state Start <<choice>>
        Start --> Asking : setting on
        Start --> OffBackingUp : setting off, and fx's line is in init.lua
        Start --> Done : setting off and no line, or gave up before
        Asking --> WritingFxLua : Rex has no rule, fx.lua is not foreign, and not (added and line gone)
        Asking --> Done : Rex trusts fx, or no answer, or fx.lua foreign, or added and line gone
        WritingFxLua --> BackingUp : fx.lua written as ours
        BackingUp --> Comparing : init.lua copied
        Comparing --> Done : init.lua changed since the observation; delete fx.lua if this attempt created it
        Comparing --> Checking : unchanged; fx's line written (one atomic step)
        Checking --> Reloading : check passes
        Checking --> UndoingLine : check fails
        Reloading --> Verifying : reload done
        Reloading --> UndoingLine : reload fails
        Verifying --> Done : Rex trusts fx; added set
        Verifying --> UndoingLine : Rex untrusted or no_rule (gave up), or no answer
        UndoingLine --> DeletingFxLua : take out only the line this attempt wrote, never put one back
        DeletingFxLua --> UndoingReload : delete fx.lua if this attempt created it
        UndoingReload --> Done : reload (failure ignored)
        OffBackingUp --> OffComparing : init.lua copied
        OffComparing --> Done : init.lua changed since the observation; nothing else changes
        OffComparing --> OffChecking : unchanged; fx's line removed (one atomic step)
        OffChecking --> OffDeletingFxLua : check result is only logged
        OffDeletingFxLua --> OffReloadClear : delete fx.lua if the observation had it as ours
        OffReloadClear --> Done : reload (failure ignored), then added cleared
    }
